                <pb facs="0744" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1241: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-15T12:00:00+08:00">September 15,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 15—3:09 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1096. My 1091, September 13, 9 p.m. Following just received from Shanghai: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“September 14, 2 p.m.</p>
                        <p>Your September 13, 7 p.m. Consular body meeting will probably be held on
                            September 20th.</p>
                        <p>2. J. K. Choy, Shanghai
                            Commissioner of Finance and one of the two Chinese negotiators of the
                            extra-Settlement road[s] agreement, informs me that yesterday Brenan told Mayor Wu and himself informally
                            that the British are unwilling to proceed with the agreement in the face
                            of the Japanese opposition.</p>
                        <p>Not repeated to the Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
